==Solution 7 (Pythagorean Theorem)==
[[File:2022 AMC 12A 24.png|360px|right]]
Consider the reflection <imath>P^{\prime}</imath> of <imath>P</imath> over the perpendicular bisector of <imath>\overline{BC}</imath>. 
<cmath>PB = P^{\prime}C = a, PC = P^{\prime}B = b.</cmath>
Let <imath>PE \perp BC, P^{\prime}E^{\prime} \perp BC.</imath>
<cmath>BE = CE^{\prime}, PP^{\prime} = EE^{\prime} \implies </cmath>
<cmath>b^2 - a^2 = PC^2 - PB^2 = CE^2 - BE^2</cmath>
<cmath>=(CE - BE)(CE + BE) = EE^{\prime} \cdot BC = PP^{\prime} \cdot BC.</cmath>
Similarly,
<cmath>d^2 - c^2 = PP^{\prime} \cdot AD \implies \frac {BC}{AD} = \frac {b^2 - a^2}{d^2 - c^2}= \boxed{\textbf{(B) }\frac{1}{3}}.</cmath>
